d Fever: less likely due to extreme leukocytosis and elevated LAP", "Endocrine Emergency (Hypercalcemia/Adrenal Insufficiency): normal calcium (10.9 mEq/L is borderline high but not diagnostic) and no hypoglycemia", "Malignancy with Constitutional Features (e.g., Lymphoma): considered possible but ranked lower than systemic infection/myeloproliferative disorders due to incomplete evidence"], "alarm_features": ["Weight loss (constitutional alarm sign)", "Leukocytosis (66,500/mm³ with elevated alk phosphatase) (systemic alarm sign)", "New systolic murmur (possible systemic pathology)"]}, "branches": {"B1": {"id": "B1", "label": "Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.25, "posterior": 0.11415525114155252, "danger": 0.9, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["The complete absence of blasts in peripheral blood and normal differential strongly excludes blast-containing myeloid neoplasms (B1), which would typically sho…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.0, "interrupt_relevance": 0.8, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B2": {"id": "B2", "label": "Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "expanded", "prior": 0.0, "posterior": 0.5753424657534246, "danger": 0.6, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.5, "evidence_for": ["Elevated LAP and subacute constitutional symptoms are characteristic of chronic myeloid disorders (e.g., CML) rather than acute leukemias or reactive leukocyto…"], "evidence_against": ["While splenomegaly can occur in chronic myeloproliferative disorders, its absence alone (with elevated LAP and constitutional symptoms) does not decisively ref…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": ["B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3"], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.2, "interrupt_relevance": 0.4, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "urgency"}, "B3": {"id": "B3", "label": "Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "reopened", "prior": 0.1, "posterior": 0.09132420091324202, "danger": 0.8, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 2, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.0, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B4": {"id": "B4", "label": "Lymphoproliferative / Plasma Cell Disorder", "parent": "ROOT", "level": 1, "status": "live", "prior": 0.15, "posterior": 0.136986301369863, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP and subacute constitutional symptoms are characteristic of chronic myeloid disorders (e.g., CML) rather than acute leukemias or reactive leukocyto…"], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.25, "interrupt_relevance": 0.2, "level_role": "family", "classification_axis": "mechanism"}, "B5": {"id": "B5", "label": "Reactive / Non-malignant Leukocytosis", "level": 1, "status": "parked", "posterior": 0.082, "danger": 0.3, "parent": "ROOT", "closure_reason": "", "evidence_against": ["Elevated LAP and subacute constitutional symptoms are characteristic of chronic myeloid disorders (e.g., CML) rather than acute leukemias or reactive leukocyto…"]}, "B2.1": {"id": "B2.1", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Chronic Phase (CML-chronic)", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.3452054794520548, "posterior": 0.3452054794520548, "danger": 0.7, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.3, "interrupt_relevance": 0.7, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2.2": {"id": "B2.2", "label": "Polycythemia Vera (PV)", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.1726027397260274, "posterior": 0.1726027397260274, "danger": 0.4, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.0, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.25, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "specific_disease", "classification_axis": "etiology"}, "B2.3": {"id": "B2.3", "label": "Other Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasms (e.g., Essential Thrombocythemia, Myelofibrosis)", "parent": "B2", "level": 2, "status": "live", "prior": 0.05753424657534247, "posterior": 0.05753424657534247, "danger": 0.5, "actionability": 0.0, "explanatory_coverage": 0.0, "expand_score": 0.0, "evidence_for": [], "evidence_against": [], "unresolved_questions": [], "children": [], "closure_reason": "", "turn_cost_to_refine": 1.5, "diagnosis_commitment_gain": 0.15, "interrupt_relevance": 0.3, "level_role": "disease_class", "classification_axis": "anatomy"}}, "frontier": ["B1", "B2.1", "B2.2", "B2.3", "B4", "B3"], "other_mass": 0.0, "pending_results": [], "actions_taken": [{"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the extreme leukocytosis (66k) with elevated LAP represent a distinguishing biomarker pattern supporting Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts over reactive processes?", "summary": "The extreme leukocytosis and elevated LAP are inconsistent with a blast-associated myeloid neoplasm (B1) due to normal differential counts. These findings are more specific to chronic clonal myeloproliferative conditions like CML."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the combination of subacute constitutional symptoms and a normal peripheral blood differential with elevated LAP align better with Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm over reactive leukocytosis?", "summary": "Elevated LAP and subacute constitutional symptoms are characteristic of chronic myeloid disorders (e.g., CML) rather than acute leukemias or reactive leukocytosis, supporting the B2 hypothesis."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the normal peripheral blood differential without blasts argue more strongly against Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts than against other branches like Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm?", "summary": "The complete absence of blasts in peripheral blood and normal differential strongly excludes blast-containing myeloid neoplasms (B1), which would typically show blasts in the blood, and moderately favors chronic myeloproliferative processes (B2)."}, {"t": 1, "type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "content": "Does the absence of physical exam findings for splenomegaly challenge Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasm as the primary diagnosis despite elevated LAP?", "summary": "While splenomegaly can occur in chronic myeloproliferative disorders, its absence alone (with elevated LAP and constitutional symptoms) does not decisively refute B2, as early-stage CML may not yet manifest splenomegaly."}], "differential_history": [{"top": [["B2", 0.575], ["B2.1", 0.345], ["B2.2", 0.173]]}], "deliberation": {}, "interrupt": {"active": false, "reason": "Case does not meet universal instability markers (airway, respiratory, or hemodynamic compromise, uncontrolled hemorrhage) or time-critical syndrome patterns (STEMI, septic shock, tension pneumothorax, stroke, or meningitis with herniation risk). Patient is stable with no end-organ signs despite elevated WBC.", "required_actions": []}, "termination": {"ready_to_stop": false, "termination_type": "continue", "reason": "Leading hypothesis (B2.1: CML-chronic) posterior (34.5%) remains below 0.75 AND dangerous alternatives (B1: myeloid blasts, posterior 11.4% and danger 0.9) exist. Further discriminators (e.g., JAK2 mutation, Philadelphia chromosome testing, bone marrow assessment) are untried and could significantly increase confidence."}, "turn_budget_used": 1, "estimated_remaining_value": 0.9, "max_turn_budget": 5, "latest_action_type": "ANALYZE_VIGNETTE", "diagnosis_readiness_score": 0.3452054794520548, "benchmark_output_ready": false, "static_question": "Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?", "static_options": [{"id": "A", "description": "Acute lymphoblastic lymphoma"}, {"id": "B", "description": "Chronic lymphocytic leukemia"}, {"id": "C", "description": "Chronic myeloid leukemia"}, {"id": "D", "description": "Leukemoid reaction"}, {"id": "E", "description": "Multiple myeloma"}], "seen_evidence_ids": [], "seen_evidence_phenotypes": "{'Myeloproliferative disorder'}", "mode_policy": {"benchmark_purity": true, "allow_external_knowledge": true}, "answer_option_mapping": {}, "tool_use_log": [], "root_revision_needed": false, "max_tree_depth": 3, "reasoning_ledger": {"anchor": {"hypothesis": "B2", "t": 0, "posterior_at_anchor": 0.575}, "leader": {"branch_id": "B2.1", "label": "Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Chronic Phase (CML-chronic)", "posterior": 0.345, "leading_since_t": 0, "n_revisions": 0}, "leader_evidence": {"confirming": 0, "disconfirming": 0, "last_disconfirming_digest": ""}, "action_intents": [{"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}, {"t": 1, "intent": "broaden"}], "considered_alternatives": ["B2.2", "B4", "B1"]}, "discriminator_hints": "[Knowledge Layer: coverage=71%, source=both]\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts:\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, decreased circulating antibody level\n  Favours second: abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Chronic Phase (CML-chronic):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, elevated serum creatinine, functional abnormality of the gastrointestinal tract\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Polycythemia Vera (PV):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, decreased circulating antibody level, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, blurred vision, burning sensation in extremities\n\nMyeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Other Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasms (e.g., Essential Thrombocythemia, Myelofibrosis):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of the bladder, abnormality of vitamin b12 metabolism, acute kidney injury, bone pain, elevated serum creatinine\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Chronic Phase (CML-chronic):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal swelling, abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Polycythemia Vera (PV):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n\nLymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts vs Other Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasms (e.g., Essential Thrombocythemia, Myelofibrosis):\n  Favours first:  abnormality of skin physiology, abnormality of the endocrine system, acrocyanosis, areflexia, arterial thrombosis\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia in Chronic Phase (CML-chronic) vs Polycythemia Vera (PV):\n  Favours first:  abdominal swelling, abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia\n  Favours second: abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, burning sensation in extremities, confusion\n\nChronic Myeloid Leukemia in Chronic Phase (CML-chronic) vs Other Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasms (e.g., Essential Thrombocythemia, Myelofibrosis):\n  Favours first:  abdominal swelling, bleeding easily, blurred vision, bone pain, enlarged spleen\n\nPolycythemia Vera (PV) vs Other Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasms (e.g., Essential Thrombocythemia, Myelofibrosis):\n  Favours first:  abdominal pain, abnormal erythrocyte morphology, bleeding gums, blurred vision, bone pain\n  Favours second: abnormal bronchus physiology, abnormal cd4:cd8 ratio, absent speech, agammaglobulinemia, anorexia\n\nRelated to Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: cd4+/cd56+ hematodermic neoplasm, hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, mast cell neoplasm\n\nRelated to Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts: hematopoietic and lymphoid cell neoplasm, lymphoid leukemia (disease), lymphoma\n\nRelated to Chronic Myeloid Leukemia in Chronic Phase (CML-chronic): myelodysplastic/myeloproliferative disease, myelodysplastic/myeloproliferative neoplasm\n\nRelated to Polycythemia Vera (PV): acquired secondary polycythemia, congenital secondary polycythemia, polycythemia (disease)\n\nRelated to Other Chronic Myeloproliferative Neoplasms (e.g., Essential Thrombocythemia, Myelofibrosis): bone marrow cancer, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, chronic eosinophilic leukemia, not otherwise specified\n\n[Indirect reasoning chains (PrimeKG 2-hop):]\n  A 59-year-old man presents to his primary care physician for fatigue → fatigue → Myeloid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts\n  A 59-year-old man presents to his primary care physician for fatigue → fatigue → Lymphoid Neoplasm with Increased Blasts"}
